load 0
=== options
--- mplayer -fs
-fs 	play full screen
-fstype 	the full-screen modes, in order (X11)
--- mplayer -sub
-sub 	subtitle files (,-separated)
-sub-bg-alpha 	the opacity of the subtitles' background (0 to 255)
-sub-bg-color 	the subtitles' background (0 to 255)
-sub-demuxer 	the demuxer of -subfile
-sub-fuzziness 	which subtitle files to load
-sub-paths 	more directories to look for subtitles in (,-separated)
-subalign 	which edge of the subtitles is at -subpos
-subcc 	show the DVD closed captions of a channel (1 to 8)
-subcp 	the code page of the subtitles (enca:LANG:FALLBACK: guess it)
-subdelay 	the subtitle delay
-subfile 	a subtitle file of a format that has a demuxer
-subfont 	the subtitle font (a font file, or a fontconfig pattern)
-subfont-autoscale 	how the text is scaled
-subfont-blur 	the font's blur radius (0 to 8)
-subfont-encoding 	the font's encoding
-subfont-osd-scale 	the size of the OSD (0 to 100)
-subfont-outline 	the font's outline width (0 to 8)
-subfont-text-scale 	the size of subtitle text (0 to 100)
-subfps 	the frame rate of the subtitle file
-subpos 	the subtitles' height (0 to 150, 100: the bottom)
-subwidth 	the subtitles' width (10 to 100)
--- mplayer -nos
-noslices 	draw the video whole, not in bands
-nosound 	play no audio
-nostop-xscreensaver 	don't turn off the screensaver while playing
-nosub 	don't show subtitles from the file
=== values
--- mplayer -vo 
gl 	OpenGL
gl_nosw 	OpenGL no software rendering
sdl 	SDL YUV/RGB/BGR renderer (SDL v1.1.7+ only!)
x11 	X11 ( XImage/Shm )
xover 	General X11 driver for overlay capable video output drivers
xv 	X11/Xv
--- mplayer -vo xv,
xv,gl 	OpenGL
xv,gl_nosw 	OpenGL no software rendering
xv,sdl 	SDL YUV/RGB/BGR renderer (SDL v1.1.7+ only!)
xv,x11 	X11 ( XImage/Shm )
xv,xover 	General X11 driver for overlay capable video output drivers
--- mplayer -vo gl:yuv=2,x
gl:yuv=2,x11 	X11 ( XImage/Shm )
gl:yuv=2,xover 	General X11 driver for overlay capable video output drivers
gl:yuv=2,xv 	X11/Xv
--- mplayer -ao p
pulse 	PulseAudio audio output
--- mplayer -vf 
bmovl 	Read bitmaps from a FIFO and display them in window
crop 	cropping
expand 	expanding & osd
format 	force output format
rectangle 	draw rectangle
scale 	software scaling
vo 	libvo wrapper
yadif 	Yet Another DeInterlacing Filter
--- mplayer -vf scale=640:480,y
scale=640:480,yadif 	Yet Another DeInterlacing Filter
--- mplayer -vf scale=
--- mplayer -af-add v
volume 	Volume control audio filter
--- mplayer -vc ffh
ffh264 	FFmpeg H.264
ffhevc 	FFmpeg HEVC / H.265
--- mplayer -vc -ffh264,ffh
-ffh264,ffhevc 	FFmpeg HEVC / H.265
--- mplayer -ac wma9
wma9dmo 	Windows Media Audio 9 DMO
wma9spdmo 	Windows Media Audio 9 Speech DMO
wma9spdshow 	Windows Media Audio 9 Speech DShow
--- mplayer -vfm 
black 	black video generator (no decoding, always outputs black frames)
ffmpeg 	FFmpeg's libavcodec codec family (native codecs)
null 	Null video decoder (no decoding)
theora 	Theora/VP3 (Theora project's VP3 codec)
--- mplayer -afm hw
hwac3 	AC3/DTS pass-through S/PDIF
hwmpa 	MPEG audio pass-through (fake decoder) (For hardware decoders)
--- mplayer -demuxer 
avi 	AVI demuxer (AVI files, including non interleaved files)
lavf 	libavformat demuxer (supports many formats, requires libavformat)
lavfpref 	libavformat preferred demuxer (supports many formats, requires libavformat)
mf 	mf demuxer (multiframe?, pictures demuxer)
mkv 	Matroska demuxer
rawaudio 	Raw audio demuxer
rawvideo 	Raw video demuxer
tv 	Tv card demuxer (?)
--- mplayer -demuxer +m
+mf 	mf demuxer (multiframe?, pictures demuxer)
+mkv 	Matroska demuxer
--- mplayer -sub-demuxer l
lavf 	libavformat demuxer (supports many formats, requires libavformat)
lavfpref 	libavformat preferred demuxer (supports many formats, requires libavformat)
--- mplayer -profile 
fast 	no frills
hq 	
--- mplayer -profile fast,
fast,hq 	
--- mplayer -show-profile h
hq 	
--- mplayer -sws 
0 	fast bilinear
1 	bilinear
10 	natural bicubic spline
2 	bicubic (default)
3 	experimental
4 	nearest neighbour
5 	area
6 	luma bicubic, chroma bilinear
7 	gauss
8 	sincR
9 	lanczos
--- mplayer -osdlevel 
0 	subtitles only
1 	volume and seek (default)
2 	volume, seek, time and percentage
3 	volume, seek, time, percentage and total time
--- mplayer -fstype layer,s
layer,stays_on_top 	_NETWM_STATE_STAYS_ON_TOP
--- mplayer -sub movie.srt,movie.a
movie.srt,movie.ass 
--- mplayer -sub-paths subs/
subs/en/
--- mplayer -ss 
--- mplayer -ss 10 m
movie.ass 
movie.mkv 
movie.srt 
--- mplayer -noconfig 
all 
gui 
system 
user 
